  "notes": [
    "The 2022 swap contract 0x13d8faf4a690f5ae52e2d2c52938d1167057b9af is a later version of the same BatchSwap code with the same editCounterPart path, drained by the same attack contracts in the same campaign, so its drains merge here (rule 4). The earliest self-closed swap that pulled a third party's asset is this WETH drain, a day before the main NFT drain.",
    "Campaign is every later self-closed swap with a third-party pull on either contract, except the NFT Trader deployer's own recovery from attacker contracts. BAYC and MAYC are valued at the median single-item marketplace fill around the incident (26.3 and 5.19 ETH); the other 126 NFTs from 30 collections are not valued, so the loss is a floor."
  ]
